Third-party material
--------------------
Tier A tasks are derived from OpenAPI descriptions in the APIs.guru
directory (https://apis.guru). The directory index is CC0. Each API
description keeps the terms that its owner declared.
- 3 specs carry restrictive licences: apiz.ebay.com:sell-finances,
  nfusionsolutions.biz and surevoip.co.uk. They are excluded from the
  public dataset.
- 20 of the 27 kept specs declare no licence. They stay in the dataset,
  with a note in the dataset card. Each task records its spec licence in
  the spec_license_* fields.
- The recordings and the server responses in Tier A tasks are synthetic.
  They are not copied from the real services.

Model outputs
-------------
- Beam-1.0-501B-A23B outputs (clients, transcripts, result tables) were
  produced through Reflection's API and are subject to Reflection's terms.
- GPT-OSS-120B and Qwen3.5-397B-A17B outputs were produced through the
  Hugging Face Inference Providers router. Both models are Apache-2.0.
  No model weights are redistributed.
- Model calls used the authors' Reflection API access (Beam) and the
  authors' own Hugging Face Inference Provider credits (GPT-OSS-120B,
  Qwen3.5-397B-A17B). No other funding.

Tier B (invented stateful APIs) and case 3 (API repair tasks) are fully
synthetic. They contain no third-party material.

Names of third-party tools and services (for example reverse-api-engineer,
Integuru, Hugging Face, Beam) belong to their owners and are used only to
identify them.
